						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 1: FLIPPING THE INPUT\n\nIn this example we have a Float In node running from 0 to 1.\nWe use 1-x to flip this to a 1 to 0 range.\nThis makes sense in this context as the parameter is called shrink, the more you shrink, the smaller the shape should be."
					}
				},
